   1: PRE-TABLE BLOCK -- #525 wdcaltdigin, PASS-3 CLASS CLOSURE
   2: =========================================================
   3: WRITTEN BEFORE TABLE 1 RUNS, so this file's own mtime proves the order.
   4: 
   5: WHY THIS TABLE EXISTS.  The ninth seat -- fired because check_stage_panels refused
   6: the commit at 8/9 -- BUILT `&& (odata & (WDCS_DRDY | WDCS_DRQ))` and scored it 19/19
   7: against the shipped instrument: a TOTAL ESCAPE.  The round had audited PER BIT, and
   8: every bit WAS driven both ways; but the predicate is a DISJUNCTION, whose negation
   9: (DRDY clear AND DRQ clear) held in no row.  Two consecutive passes found one class,
  10: so this repair owes the CLASS CLOSURE and this table VERIFIES THE ENUMERATION.
  11: 
  12: ------------------------------------------------------------------ THE SPACE
  13: 
  14: Mutant form:  `if (odata & X) odata = 0;`  -- guard kept, repair conditioned on
  15: status bits -- for X over the 15 nonzero subsets of {DRDY 0x40, DSC 0x10, DRQ 0x08,
  16: ERR 0x01}, the four bits status_byte() can set.
  17: 
  18: Reachable statuses: DRDY and DSC are set TOGETHER (only under diskimage_exist);
  19: DRQ and ERR are independent.  So {0x00,0x50} x {0,0x08} x {0,0x01}:
  20:     0x00 0x01 0x08 0x09 0x50 0x51 0x58 0x59
  21: 
  22: A mutant ESCAPES iff (s & X) != 0 at EVERY CORE status s -- it then zeroes exactly
  23: where the fix does.
  24: 
  25: ------------------------------------------------------ CORE ROWS AND THEIR STATUS
  26: 
  27:     status  CORE row (offset 1, want 0x00)   status proven by
  28:     0x51    CORE_READ_OFF1_POWERON    s1     CONTROL_STATUS_POWERON  a3
  29:     0x58    CORE_READ_OFF1_ARMED      s4     CONTROL_STATUS_ARMED    s2
  30:     0x08    CORE_READ_OFF1_EMPTYSLAVE t6     CONTROL_STATUS_EMPTYSLAVE t4
  31:     0x01    CORE_READ_OFF1_PWR_SLAVE  k0 NEW CONTROL_STATUS_PWR_SLAVE  t7 NEW
  32:     0x50    CORE_READ_OFF1_SRST       k1 NEW WRITE0_SRST_DRQ_CLEAR   s5
  33: 
  34: Every status is MEASURED by a row of its own, so the enumeration below is grounded
  35: in observed values, not in assumed device behaviour.  Probe BASE: 22/22 CONTROL=OK.
  36: 
  37: ------------------------------------------------------- THE ENUMERATION (derived)
  38: 
  39: DIE -- 12 of 15:
  40:    DRDY          0x40   killed at 0x08 (t6), 0x01 (k0)
  41:    DSC           0x10   killed at 0x08 (t6), 0x01 (k0)
  42:    DRDY|DSC      0x50   killed at 0x08 (t6), 0x01 (k0)
  43:    DRQ           0x08   killed at 0x51 (s1), 0x01 (k0), 0x50 (k1)
  44:    DRDY|DRQ      0x48   killed at 0x01 (k0) ONLY      <- M_DRDYDRQ, the measured escape
  45:    DSC|DRQ       0x18   killed at 0x01 (k0) ONLY
  46:    DRDY|DSC|DRQ  0x58   killed at 0x01 (k0) ONLY
  47:    ERR           0x01   killed at 0x58 (s4), 0x08 (t6), 0x50 (k1)
  48:    DRDY|ERR      0x41   killed at 0x08 (t6) ONLY
  49:    DSC|ERR       0x11   killed at 0x08 (t6) ONLY
  50:    DRDY|DSC|ERR  0x51   killed at 0x08 (t6) ONLY
  51:    DRQ|ERR       0x09   killed at 0x50 (k1) ONLY      <- M_DRQERR, the measured escape
  52: 
  53: SURVIVE -- 3 of 15, ALL EQUIVALENT:
  54:    DRDY|DRQ|ERR  0x49 } each differs from the fix only at status 0x00 (leak 0x00 ==
  55:    DSC|DRQ|ERR   0x19 } decline 0x00, indistinguishable) or 0x10 (DSC without DRDY,
  56:    all four      0x59 } unreachable).  No reachable, observable difference exists.
  57: 
  58: SOLE CARRIERS, disclosed (the L3 shape): k0 is the only killer of 3 masks, t6 of 3,
  59: k1 of 1.  That is inherent to a closure where each cell is ONE status value; a
  60: second row per cell would re-test the same status and add no discrimination.
  61: 
  62: ------------------------------------------------------------------ TABLE LEGS
  63: 
  64:   BASE        the fix                                   predict 22/22
  65:   HEAD        the committed dev_wdc.c (clause a)         predict RED on the CORE rows
  66:   M_DRDY      X = 0x40  (the round's own pass-2 mutant)  predict DIE  (t6, k0)
  67:   M_DRDYDRQ   X = 0x48  (the ninth seat's escape)        predict DIE  (k0 only)
  68:   M_DRQERR    X = 0x09  (the second cell)                predict DIE  (k1 only)
  69:   E_EQUIV49   X = 0x49  (predicted EQUIVALENT)           predict SURVIVE 22/22
  70: 
  71: The last leg makes the arithmetic FALSIFIABLE IN BOTH DIRECTIONS: if it dies, the
  72: equivalence derivation is wrong and the reachable-status set is not what status_byte()
