The audit gives 12 killed masks and 3 equivalent survivors, with every recorded failure on a CORE read whose byte can change. I found two qualifications to the write-up: the equivalence explanation omits the unreachable `0x40` case, and the claimed width clamp depends on `memory_rw.c`, which is outside the four-file reading scope.
